' fieldemon_macros.bas
' Part of: fieldemon
' VBA module for Davidson Group ringing data workbook
' Provides live error checking and ring number shortcut
'
' HOW TO INSTALL:
' 1. Open your .xlsm workbook in Excel
' 2. Press Alt+F11 to open the VBA editor
' 3. In the Project panel, find your workbook and expand it
' 4. Right-click on "Microsoft Excel Objects" > "ThisWorkbook"
'    and paste the Workbook_Open code there
' 5. Right-click on the sheet named "Ringing data" in the Project panel
'    and paste the Worksheet_Change code there
' 6. Right-click on "Modules" > "Insert" > "Module"
'    and paste everything else into that module
' 7. Close the VBA editor and save the workbook as .xlsm
'
' SHEETS REQUIRED:
'   "Ringing data"  - main data entry sheet
'   "Individuals"   - generated by build_individuals_table.py
'   "Species list"  - manually maintained (see setup instructions below)
'
' SPECIES LIST SHEET SETUP:
'   Create a sheet called "Species list" with these columns:
'   A: species code (e.g. BLUTI)
'   B: common name (e.g. blue tit)
'   C: ring size (e.g. A)
'   D: min wing (e.g. 58)
'   E: max wing (e.g. 68)
'   F: min weight (e.g. 8)
'   G: max weight (e.g. 12)
'   Row 1 = headers, data starts row 2
'
'   Starter data (copy into the sheet):
'   Code    Name                        Ring  MinW  MaxW  MinWt MaxWt
'   BLUTI   blue tit                    A     58    68    8     12
'   GRETI   great tit                   A     69    81    14.5  21
'   ROBIN   robin                       A     68    79    13    24
'   LOTTI   long-tailed tit             AA    56    64    6     9
'   COATI   coal tit                    A     56    64    7     10
'   DUNNO   dunnock                     B     64    75    16    25
'   NUTHA   nuthatch                    B     78    89    18    25
'   GRSWO   great spotted woodpecker    C     125   139   66    90
'   CHAFF   chaffinch                   A     75    94    16    26
'   GOLDF   goldfinch                   A     72    84    12    18
'   BLACA   blackcap                    A     69    79    13    22
'   BLABI   blackbird                   C     119   141   74    129
'   BULLF   bullfinch                   A     76    87    18    26
'   MARTI   marsh tit                   A     57    67    9     12
'   WREN    wren                        AA    43    54    7     12
'   CHIFF   chiffchaff                  AA    51    67    5     9
'   GOLDC   goldcrest                   AA    48    57    4     6
'   TREEC   treecreeper                 AA    57    68    6     10
'   REDWI   redwing                     CC    110   130   48    90
'   SONTH   song thrush                 CC    111   127   55    93
'   GARWA   garden warbler              A     68    78    12    22
'   REDPO   redpoll                     A     68    78    10    18
' ============================================================================

